WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.258 --> 00:00:02.204
- I'm just gonna like throw out my phone,

00:00:02.204 --> 00:00:03.895
I don't need you anymore.

00:00:03.895 --> 00:00:05.958
Just kidding, I
desperately still need you.

00:00:05.958 --> 00:00:09.041
(playful band music)

00:00:11.006 --> 00:00:12.977
- This week, we are
trying to detach ourselves

00:00:12.977 --> 00:00:15.154
from our phones using wearable technology.

00:00:15.154 --> 00:00:17.089
- My personal struggle is just the anxiety

00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:19.508
of constantly checking for messages

00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:21.371
from certain individuals.

00:00:21.371 --> 00:00:23.108
- I wanna try to curb the mindlessness

00:00:23.108 --> 00:00:25.412
of just opening my phone
and swiping through.

00:00:25.412 --> 00:00:27.977
- I'm on my phone before I
go to sleep, when I wake up,

00:00:27.977 --> 00:00:29.768
at work, with my friends.

00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:31.308
I'm just always on my phone.

00:00:31.308 --> 00:00:32.593
- Didn't even think about it,

00:00:32.593 --> 00:00:35.607
I just opened my phone
and went to my email.

00:00:35.607 --> 00:00:38.343
- I sometimes see myself
missing parts of conversations.

00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:41.555
- It is connecting me with
all these other people,

00:00:41.555 --> 00:00:42.842
and not connecting me with the person

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.425
that's sitting right next to me.

00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:47.718
- To track how much I use my phone,

00:00:47.718 --> 00:00:50.454
we downloaded the Moment app.

00:00:50.454 --> 00:00:53.562
- Yesterday, I used my phone
for five hours and 23 minutes.

00:00:53.562 --> 00:00:54.678
- Five Hours.

00:00:54.678 --> 00:00:57.324
- Three hours and 11 minutes.

00:00:57.324 --> 00:00:58.495
That's really scary.

00:00:58.495 --> 00:01:01.495
(upbeat rock music)

00:01:03.358 --> 00:01:05.985
- Listen,
- It's very stylish.

00:01:05.985 --> 00:01:08.985
- I'll set it for voice and texting.

00:01:09.972 --> 00:01:11.880
- So, probably one for my mom, and my dad.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.519
- Maybe my mother, if she calls.

00:01:13.519 --> 00:01:15.074
Now that I'm saying that out loud,

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:19.043
I don't need to be checking
my phone all that often, huh.

00:01:19.043 --> 00:01:21.445
- I'm hoping that this ring will serve as

00:01:21.445 --> 00:01:25.612
when you tie something around
your finger to not forget.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.618
- Three and a half hours of my
life, I want that time back.

00:01:33.618 --> 00:01:35.895
I just set up my Ringly and
it's already annoying me

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.640
because it's just vibrating

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.586
while I'm just trying to get work done.

00:01:39.586 --> 00:01:41.806
I don't need to know when my mom texts me

00:01:41.806 --> 00:01:44.609
asking what Tanya from
High School is up to.

00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:47.001
- It's been cool feeling
all the notifications,

00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:49.540
but then I'll absolutely
check when they're happening.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.699
- Moment app takes up
a lot of battery space,

00:01:51.699 --> 00:01:53.950
so I'm actually using my phone less

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.643
because my phone's dying.

00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:56.932
- I just got home from work,

00:01:56.932 --> 00:01:59.023
and I've been on my phone for 45 minutes,

00:01:59.023 --> 00:02:00.561
I didn't even realize it.

00:02:00.561 --> 00:02:01.728
I'm a failure.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.969
- My phone has made me aware of me

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:08.716
waking up and checking my email,

00:02:08.716 --> 00:02:11.519
and text messages right away.

00:02:11.519 --> 00:02:14.177
- So, I'm at the doctor's,
and I'm really bored,

00:02:14.177 --> 00:02:16.999
but I brought a magazine with me today

00:02:16.999 --> 00:02:19.255
because I figured I'm gonna be on my phone

00:02:19.255 --> 00:02:22.916
so I brought something to
read and it's kind of helping.

00:02:22.916 --> 00:02:25.167
- I've only been on for about two hours,

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:28.185
and it's now currently around
3 PM in the afternoon, so,

00:02:28.185 --> 00:02:30.740
I think that's already a lot
less than what I've been using.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:32.242
- The Ringly doesn't help me from

00:02:32.242 --> 00:02:34.773
wanting to scroll through my
phone while I'm watching TV,

00:02:34.773 --> 00:02:37.003
and it reminds me of the text
messages that I'm getting

00:02:37.003 --> 00:02:41.573
while I'm watching TV, so it's
not super helpful with that.

00:02:41.573 --> 00:02:45.740
Numbers from my phone have
only gone down like 30 minutes.

00:02:46.675 --> 00:02:49.774
- I'm at a show right now, and
this friend is on her phone,

00:02:49.774 --> 00:02:51.773
and this friend is on her phone.

00:02:51.773 --> 00:02:52.801
Everyone's on their phone,

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.993
and I'm not allowed to be on my phone.

00:02:54.993 --> 00:02:57.278
- The Ringly was awesome
in a meeting today,

00:02:57.278 --> 00:02:59.639
because I have Google
Calendar alerts set up,

00:02:59.639 --> 00:03:01.510
and it buzzed when it was 15 minutes

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:02.642
towards the end of the hour,

00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:06.394
so I knew it was time to get
things going and finish up,

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:07.663
and it was a great moment

00:03:07.663 --> 00:03:09.831
without having to look at my phone.

00:03:09.831 --> 00:03:10.823
- So, I'm laying in bed

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.992
and all I want to do is check Instagram,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.979
but I can't be on my phone right now,

00:03:14.979 --> 00:03:17.084
so I'm gonna just try to go to sleep,

00:03:17.084 --> 00:03:18.813
but I'm just constantly thinking about

00:03:18.813 --> 00:03:21.413
what is happening on
Instagram Story right now.

00:03:21.413 --> 00:03:25.580
- This feels like I'm being
nannied by an app on my phone.

00:03:26.425 --> 00:03:28.308
So, it's Thursday, and I just woke up,

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.533
and I just looked at my phone to see

00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:32.333
what my numbers were yesterday,

00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.306
and I guess on Wednesday I went down

00:03:34.306 --> 00:03:37.556
from three hours to two and half hours,

00:03:38.474 --> 00:03:42.850
which isn't great, but
I'm making progress.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:43.954
- So, I'm sitting outside,

00:03:43.954 --> 00:03:45.864
and I haven't picked up my phone once.

00:03:45.864 --> 00:03:48.050
- There's this guy, and
I'm trying not to text,

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.913
and I'm trying not to be
anxious, but, whatever.

00:03:50.913 --> 00:03:55.080
And, it's a much better method
of not looking at your phone.

00:03:56.114 --> 00:03:57.726
Like, this is the first
time I've looked at my phone

00:03:57.726 --> 00:03:59.405
in maybe five hours all day.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.666
- Just went to the market,
and it took me half the time,

00:04:01.666 --> 00:04:04.733
'cause I wasn't checking
text messages the whole time.

00:04:04.733 --> 00:04:08.116
- I sit outside, and not talk
to anyone for three hours,

00:04:08.116 --> 00:04:09.485
which feels amazing.

00:04:09.485 --> 00:04:12.022
- If you really want to
stop looking at your phone,

00:04:12.022 --> 00:04:13.614
find yourself someone to crush on.

00:04:13.614 --> 00:04:14.830
- So, the week's over, and I feel like,

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:16.971
now I have a much more
healthy relationship

00:04:16.971 --> 00:04:18.691
with my phone than I did before.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.108
- I went from being on
my phone for five hours

00:04:21.108 --> 00:04:23.644
to being on my phone for
an hour and 50 minutes.

00:04:23.644 --> 00:04:25.419
- Three hours and 40 minutes.

00:04:25.419 --> 00:04:27.470
- One hour and 15 minutes a day.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.605
- I've never stayed off
my phone for that long.

00:04:29.605 --> 00:04:31.510
- It feels so light, and free.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.645
- Instead of Snapchatting on my commute,

00:04:33.645 --> 00:04:35.305
I was actually taking in the city

00:04:35.305 --> 00:04:37.306
and talking with my friends more,

00:04:37.306 --> 00:04:38.719
hanging out with my roommate more.

00:04:38.719 --> 00:04:40.032
It gave me a whole new sense

00:04:40.032 --> 00:04:42.668
of the life I was missing
outside of my phone.

00:04:42.668 --> 00:04:44.955
- Probably just tied a
string around my finger

00:04:44.955 --> 00:04:46.213
and called it a day.

00:04:46.213 --> 00:04:50.325
- I would recommend just
actual, intentional motivation

00:04:50.325 --> 00:04:52.521
to just curb your phone usage

00:04:52.521 --> 00:04:54.411
rather than relying on
a piece of technology.

00:04:54.411 --> 00:04:58.136
- What am I gonna do
with all that time now?

00:04:58.136 --> 00:05:01.636
I don't know, maybe I'll take up knitting.

